3 Defining Classes
==================

Use ‘defclass’ to define a new class.  The first argument is the class
name.  The second argument is a list of slot specifications.  Each slot
specification is a list containing the slot name and optional keyword
arguments such as :initform, :accessor, :allocation, etc.

   The third argument is optional and specifies methods directly within
the class definition (see *note Defining Methods::).


File: introduction.info,  Node: Defining Methods,  Next: Inheritance and Slots,  Prev: Defining Classes,  Up: Editing Classes.Defs

4 Defining Methods
==================

Methods can be defined inside the class definition using the :methods
keyword or separately with ‘defmethod’.

     (defmethod Player::attack ((self Player) (target Enemy))
       ;; attack logic
       )


